Hi:

Here's one approach:

g1 <- ggplot(dd, aes(x = xv))
g2 <- g1 + geom_density(data = subset(dd, set == 1)) +
                 scale_x_continuous(breaks = c(-2, 0, 2))
g3 <- g1 + geom_density(data = subset(dd, set == 2)) +
                 scale_x_continuous(breaks = c(-600, 0, 600))
library(gridExtra)
grid.arrange(g2, g3, nrow = 1)

HTH,
Dennis

